## So what?

Three published errors in three days share one shape: **prose written from a narrative rather than from the artifact the run produced.** The numbers were correct and on disk every time. The morning-of warning didn't prevent the 09-07 error, so the mitigation can't be another warning — I seeded a findings-lint topic instead (fail on placeholder tokens; fail on a window quoted without its γ; require every table row to be greppable in its named `_output.txt`). Make the correct path the short path.

The most expensive thing today wasn't either error — it was the silent visitor track. That's the track that caught the site-wide version of this same failure from outside, twice.
